<Docs title="API reference" active="API reference">
  <div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">REFERENCE / 04</span><h1>API reference</h1><p>Stable shapes for decisions, delegation, audit, and integrations.</p></div>
  <h2>AuthZEN decision request</h2><div class="doc-code">POST /access/v1/evaluation<br /><br />&#123;<br />  "subject": &#123; "type": "Agent", "id": "support-copilot" &#125;,<br />  "action": &#123; "type": "Action", "name": "tickets.read" &#125;,<br />  "resource": &#123; "type": "Ticket", "id": "4420" &#125;<br />&#125;</div>
  <h2>Decision response</h2><div class="doc-code">&#123;<br />  "decision": "Permit",<br />  "metadata": &#123; "decision_id": "dec_01H...", "policy": "v14" &#125;<br />&#125;</div>
  <h2>SDKs and examples</h2><p>The TypeScript package exposes a small client for custom agent loops. Rust consumers can call the core engine directly or mount the server router. See the <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/tree/master/examples">examples on GitHub ↗</a> for Strands, Axum, and embedding patterns.</p>
  <h2>Useful commands</h2><div class="docs-table"><div><b>agentguard validate</b><span>Validate schema and policies.</span></div><div><b>agentguard sim</b><span>Evaluate a request without executing it.</span></div><div><b>agentguard audit</b><span>Inspect and verify the decision chain.</span></div><div><b>agentguard delegate</b><span>Issue a scoped delegation token.</span></div></div>
</Docs>
